# Build context for server/Dockerfile. The context is the repo ROOT (the server
# imports the same engine the browser runs, so js/ has to be in scope) — which
# means everything that makes this a *static site* is in scope too and has no
# business in a server image.
#
# Two of these entries are about safety rather than size: node_modules would
# overwrite the arm64 modules installed inside the image with whatever a Windows or
# x86 machine had lying around, and the .env rules keep a local secrets file from
# being baked into a layer where `docker history` would show it.

# --- never, under any circumstances ---
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# --- host build artefacts that must not shadow the image's own ---
node_modules
server/node_modules
npm-debug.log*

# --- the static client: served by GitHub Pages, not by this container ---
index.html
manifest.webmanifest
sw.js
css/
icons/
scripts/
*.jpg
*.png
*.md

# --- repo furniture ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.claude
LICENSE
